  "selfReview": "The strongest piece. Intro, A, B, A' and coda with Zoo's motif in every section and Badger's figure as the bookends. The voicings are audited: no held semitone or minor-ninth rubs outside the deliberate A7(b9) colour. It passes the standalone profile. Risks a producer may hear, unverified by ear: the FM tine piano and the synth brass are our own synthesis and may read slightly synthetic where exposed (the A' hits). The stop-time bar before B (about 1 s of near silence at 22.5 s) is meant as a late-night band stop but could feel like a dropout. The VSCO string swells in B are soft-attack samples and may smear the faster chord changes.",
  "licence": "Original composition (Zoora). Rendered from our own synthesis, VCSL (CC0) and MuseScore_General / FluidR3 (MIT) samples; see docs/AUDIO_LICENSES.md."
